

[38;5;231m⏺[39m Next: what a task actually is. This matters more than it looks, because in cycle 4 every field becomes a thing that
  can change, and therefore a thing that can generate a notification. A task with one field has one event type; a task
  with eight has a noisy inbox. Fields are cheap to add later and annoying to remove once data exists, so I'd rather
  start narrow.

  My recommendation is three fields beyond identity and timestamps:

  - [1mTitle[0m — obviously.
  - [1mStatus as three states[0m (todo / in progress / done) rather than a done checkbox. A checkbox gives you exactly one
    interesting event; three states give collaborators the "someone picked this up" signal, which at your scale is
    probably the single most useful thing to be notified about.
  - [1mDue date, optional.[0m This is the one I'd include despite YAGNI, because you were undecided earlier between
    collaboration-driven and time-driven notifications. Having the field costs almost nothing now and keeps the reminder
    flavor available in cycle 4 without a migration.

  I'd leave out notes, priority, tags, subtasks, and attachments. Every one of them is a pure addition later with no
  rework — none of them changes the shape of the model or the storage interface.

  Assignee is a deliberate omission too: there's nobody to assign to until cycle 2, and inventing a placeholder user now
  would mean guessing at the identity model we haven't designed.
